      "content_html": "Smart home provider SwitchBot launched its Connected Home Security Combo in Europe on November 17. It includes two separately available packages: a set consisting of a pan-and-tilt 2K outdoor camera and ViewStation monitor, and a combination of Vision Doorbell, Lock Ultra Max door lock, and Matter-enabled Hub Mini. On the 4.3-inch monitor, residents can view camera footage, talk to visitors, and operate a connected lock; while away, they can access it through the SwitchBot app.\n\nAccording to SwitchBot, the ViewStation kit starts at €199.99, while the doorbell-and-lock package costs €319.99. The outdoor camera stores clips locally on a separately sold microSD card; recordings from the doorbell, by contrast, can only be stored in the cloud with the paid AI Guard subscription. Calls and live footage from the doorbell are not expected to be available on the ViewStation until a later update. No date has been announced yet.",
